4719	{"artifactId":"SPEC-bfa1f6c830c53982","entry":{"id":"migrated-SPEC-bfa1f6c830c53982-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:controller","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-08-05T09:35:32.150Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"brainstorm","stage":"brainstorm","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"cl1","kind":"inventory","severity":"LOW","premise":"The insrc TUI's existing panes are implemented as PascalCase *Pane.tsx files under src/cli/panes (Daemon/Repos/Workflows/Setup, plus ModelTiers), wired into the app.tsx pane host.","evidence":"The pane files resolve as real paths in sibling probes (src/cli/panes/DaemonPane.tsx:53, src/cli/panes/ReposPane.tsx:62) and the earlier module.profile listed DaemonPane/ReposPane/WorkflowsPane/SetupPane/ModelTiersPane under src/cli/panes. The literal-filename grep returned 0 only because ripgrep scans contents, not names — the inventory holds.","action":"None — confirmed via sibling paths + the analyze bundle.","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"cl2","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon exposes a `daemon.status` IPC that the CLI daemon service consumes to infer running/stopped (getStatus throw = stopped), and the stop path sends a `daemon.shutdown` RPC rather than a process signal.","evidence":"daemon.status handler at src/daemon/index.ts:849, consumed by src/cli/services/daemon.ts:50 (rpc<DaemonStatus>('daemon.status')); daemon.shutdown at daemon/index.ts:1347 + daemon.ts:77; getStatus-throw-means-stopped shown at cli/__tests__/tui.test.ts:107; stopDaemon at command.ts:84 + DaemonPane.tsx:53. Confirmed — the status card + stopped-inference + shutdown-RPC premises hold.","action":"None — anchors resolve.","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"cl3","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon entry point that a `ps` cmdline scan would match is out/daemon/index.js (the compiled daemon binary the installer/CLI spawns).","evidence":"The daemon entry is DEFINED at src/cli/services/daemon.ts:24 as DAEMON_ENTRY = join(__dirname, '../../daemon/index.js') — i.e. the resolved absolute path ends in 'daemon/index.js' (compiled: .../out/daemon/index.js under the install root). The spec's 'out/daemon/index.js' is approximately right; the ps cmdline scan should anchor on the resolved DAEMON_ENTRY, not a hard-coded 'out/daemon/index.js' literal.","action":"Design (LLD) should ground the ps cmdline pattern on src/cli/services/daemon.ts:24 DAEMON_ENTRY (suffix 'daemon/index.js') rather than a fixed 'out/' prefix — noted, not a spec blocker.","fixability":"assisted"},{"claimId":"cl4","kind":"inventory","severity":"LOW","premise":"Exactly two physical log files exist under PATHS.logDir today — daemon.log (daemon mode) and agent.log (shared by CLI mode and MCP mode) — written via the shared logger, and they are rotated (pino-roll).","evidence":"src/shared/paths.ts:104-105 define daemonLog + agentLog under LOG_DIR; src/shared/logger.ts has three pino-roll transports (lines 66/101/130) for the daemon/cli/mcp modes, with cli+mcp both routing to agentLog (src/bin/insrc-mcp.ts:39 setLogMode('mcp')). Exactly two physical files, rotated, agent.log shared by CLI + MCP — confirmed.","action":"None — the two-file + rotation premise (the basis for collapsing to two log categories) holds.","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"cl5","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"MCP client registration/connection status is obtained by running each CLI's `mcp list` (the same mechanism mcp-register.ts uses to register the insrc MCP server).","evidence":"src/daemon/mcp-register.ts (registerMcpClients) drives `mcp list` (mcp-register.test.ts:38 isList = args[0]==='mcp' && args[1]==='list') and `mcp add` via argv arrays. The per-client registration/status mechanism the MCP section reuses exists and is confirmed.","action":"None — anchor resolves.","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"cl6","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"There is no existing debug-status IPC that enumerates the daemon's connected socket clients (label/pid/connected-at) — the spec proposes it as a NEW daemon IPC surface.","evidence":"No matches for debug-status/debugStatus/debug.status or any connected-clients/clientList/socketClients enumeration anywhere in src/ — confirming the debug-status IPC (status fields + live IPC client list) is genuinely a NEW surface the spec introduces, as claimed.","action":"None — the 'new IPC' premise is correct; design must add both the tracking + the method.","fixability":"auto"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":6},"reviewedAt":"2026-08-05T09:35:32.150Z","model":"client"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
